{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head 802a7c31345129f7dfbeda447ec8ce57ced3e843.\n\nARCHITECTURE. This is a documentation-only change to the Application Profile / Host posture contract; kernel and implementation code are unchanged. The head accurately records Hugh's ruled boundary and enumerates GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_COMMON_DIR, GIT_CONFIG*, HOME, and XDG_CONFIG_HOME. It does not, however, satisfy governing request 2996e429: the page says all environment bounding, including internal/gitstore.hermeticGitEnvironment, buys determinism rather than defence, while the request explicitly requires that existing GIT_CONFIG stripping be described as defense-in-depth, not a defended boundary. The code, mutation test, and introducing commit confirm that this helper quarantines executable Git signing/verification configuration. Correct the contract before approval.\n\nSECURITY. Placing hostile operator-controlled environment outside the threat model and naming its defence as a non-goal matches ruling 57df8d25. But calling hermeticGitEnvironment merely determinism erases an extant defense-in-depth control and may invite a future maintainer to weaken signing/verification quarantine. The claim that anyone who can set these variables can already run code as the operator is also too broad: some variables route or select configuration, and code execution depends on a relevant Git invocation and executable config knob. Ground the reason in trusted-operator authority and Git configuration's ability to select executables.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. State the distinction directly: internal/app bounds repository routing for deterministic target selection; hermeticGitEnvironment quarantines executable signing/verification configuration as defense-in-depth; neither makes hostile operator environment a defended boundary. This is shorter and matches both ruling and implementation. Do not merge this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:babc61e406d81d6406d387eacd2789520260714b","head":"802a7c31345129f7dfbeda447ec8ce57ced3e843","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9432368e955027445ce94b479d9c18b32b82c144\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d94c727233d9647f1fbd612034e48b19cd9f5ecb","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}